; The MCP server as a pure library: JSON in, JSON out, no I/O. It links the
; three engine libraries for the same reason [writ_lsp] does — an answer from a
; tool call must be an answer `writ check` would give, and a second
; implementation would be a second set of bugs.

(library
 (name writ_mcp)
 (libraries writ_data writ_syntax writ_runtime writ_json))

; The same generated version the CLI reports, for `initialize`'s serverInfo: a
; client that asks which writ it is talking to must not get a hand-kept copy.
; It lives in the library rather than beside the binary — see bin/dune.

; The leading `v` is stripped here too, and tooling/cli/dune says why — a
; `dune subst` in an opam pin substitutes the tag verbatim. The two rules are
; the same five lines because the two modules are separate by design; a shared
; library for one string would be a new node in a dependency graph the fitness
; gates check.

(rule
 (targets version.ml)
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   version.ml
   (echo
    "let v =\n  let raw = \"%{version:writ}\" in\n  if String.length raw > 1 && raw.[0] = 'v' && raw.[1] >= '0' && raw.[1] <= '9'\n  then String.sub raw 1 (String.length raw - 1)\n  else raw\n"))))
